------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY — states reproduced (read the source; reproduce them ALL, invent none)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
`Delta` is a PROP-DRIVEN PRESENTATIONAL LEAF (current/previous/metric in; settings
context from useUnits/useFormatting; NO data fetch). The web source therefore has
exactly THREE render branches, all reproduced:
  • loading  — the `loading` prop -> <Skeleton>            -> DeltaLoadingView (TSSkeleton)
  • empty    — current/previous null|non-finite -> em-dash  -> DeltaEmptyView ("—" + comparedTo)
  • content  — arrow + colour + value                       -> DeltaContentView
The generic prompt states error/stale/offline are N/A for this leaf: it has no
fetch lifecycle, so fabricating them would be silent drift (covenant #9). This is a
faithful reproduction of the source, NOT scope narrowing — the source's full state
set is {loading, empty, content} and every one renders (never a blank box).

Content sub-branches reproduced (all asserted against web Delta.test.tsx golden values):
  colour: 0->muted, neutral metric->secondary, good->emerald(success), bad->rose(danger)
  arrow : +up / -down / 0->right ; hideArrow omits glyph
  value : percent (unsigned, sign via arrow) / absolute (prefix+suffix) / both ("abs (pct)")
  edge  : previous==0 & percent -> "—" (never Infinity%); previous==0 & absolute renders
  units : suffix follows useUnits prefs (mi/km, mph/km-h, Wh/mi|Wh/km, °C/°F, bar/psi),
          currency prefix follows useFormatting; precision follows settings.

i18n keys (all resolve via P1/S10 DeltaStrings; no English literals in code):
  delta.noComparison = "No comparison data"          (web parity)
  delta.title        = "%1$@ vs %2$@"                (web "{{current}} vs {{previous}}")
  delta.a11y.increased/decreased/unchanged/loading   (VoiceOver: web arrow is aria-hidden,
                                                       so direction is spoken)

Data sources (web hooks) -> bound via the P1/S8 seam, NO direct HTTP from the view:
  useUnits / useFormatting -> DeltaEnvironment delivered by DeltaEnvironmentSource
  useTranslation           -> DeltaStrings (P1/S10)
  useUnitLabels            -> DeltaUnitLabels (local pure helper, ported)
  useCompareWindow         -> only feeds the `comparedTo` string (a plain input)

Accessibility: every state carries a VoiceOver label; content speaks direction+value
(+comparedTo) and exposes the title via accessibilityValue/.help; Dynamic Type via tokens;
TSSkeleton/TSFadeIn honour Reduce Motion. Telemetry: view.opened(surface:"Delta") once.

